      "problem": "Simplify $(5 - y) \\cdot 3 - 10$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-y)\\cdot 3-10 & = \\\\ 5\\cdot 3+(-y)\\cdot 3-10 & = \\\\ (15)+(-3y)-10 & = \\\\ 15-3y-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15-3y-10 & = \\\\ (15-10)-3y & = \\\\ 5-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
